{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc | sed -n '1,300p'; rg -n \\\"ds/next|dao\\\\.stream/next|transactor/next|tx/next|\\\\(next .*transact|\\\\(ds/next\\\" src test --glob '*.{clj,cljc,cljs}' | sed -n '1,320p'; rg -n \\\"ds/open\"'!.*:transactor|:dao.stream/type :transactor|:dao.stream/type'\"\\\\s+:transactor|transactor/open|tx/open\\\" src test --glob '*.{clj,cljc,cljs}' | sed -n '1,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.space.transactor\n     2\t  \"The `:transactor` stream: a single-writer wrapper over an explicit local\n     3\t   `dao.stream` plus an explicit intake pool of `dao.stream` writers\n     4\t   (docs/design/dao.jing.md, Publication from an agent).\n     5\t\n     6\t   Descriptor:\n     7\t\n     8\t     {:dao.stream/type :transactor\n     9\t      :local-stream s   ; must satisfy IDaoStreamReader and IDaoStreamWriter;\n    10\t                        ; supplied, never created, registered, or closed\n    11\t      :intake-pool [p]  ; non-empty; every member satisfies the dao.stream\n    12\t                        ; writer surface (stream/writer?);\n    13\t                        ; supplied, never created, registered, or closed\n    14\t      :name n}          ; optional, diagnostic only\n    15\t\n    16\t   The transactor owns transaction time. Every append! or transact! writes\n    17\t   exactly ONE atomic transaction record to the local stream\n    18\t\n    19\t     {:dao.space/transaction {:t <nonnegative-integer> :datoms [...]}}\n    20\t\n    21\t   through exactly one ds/append!, so no reader can ever observe a torn\n    22\t   transaction. t is allocated from a per-wrapper watermark: on open the\n    23\t   retained history is scanned from cursor zero (index/snapshot-datoms) and\n    24\t   the next t is derived as 0 for an empty history or 1 + the maximum\n    25\t   integer datom t otherwise. A retention gap or malformed history throws.\n    26\t   The scan is the causality boundary; a caller-supplied next-t is never\n    27\t   accepted.\n    28\t\n    29\t   Single-writer: calls through one wrapper are serialized around timestamp\n    30\t   allocation and append. The watermark is per-wrapper state, so two wrappers over\n    31\t   the same local stream each derive the same next-t and silently write\n    32\t   colliding records. That is invalid and cannot be silently coordinated\n    33\t   without shared mutable state. Use one wrapper per local stream.\n    34\t\n    35\t   publish! builds the covered indexes over the local stream and enqueues\n    36\t   them into the intake pool (dao.space.index/publish-index!). Publication\n    37\t   is explicit and acknowledges enqueuing only, never observer\n    38\t   materialization.\n    39\t\n    40\t   Closing a wrapper is per handle: it rejects further appends/transacts but\n    41\t   neither closes nor erases the local stream.\"\n    42\t  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n    43\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    44\t            [dao.stream :as ds]\n    45\t            [dao.stream :as stream])\n    46\t  #?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream])))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- entity->datoms\n    50\t  \"One datom per k/v pair, all sharing transaction time `t`. `:db/id` is\n    51\t   required: a durable log cannot mint per-batch tempids without colliding\n    52\t   across appends. Attribute order within one entity's own datoms is\n    53\t   whatever the host's map iteration yields — unspecified across platforms.\"\n    54\t  [m t]\n    55\t  (when-not (contains? m :db/id)\n    56\t    (throw (ex-info \"entity map requires :db/id\" {:entity m})))\n    57\t  (let [e (:db/id m)]\n    58\t    (mapv (fn [[a v]]\n    59\t            (let [d [e a v t datom/default-op]]\n    60\t              (when-not (datom/local-datom? d)\n    61\t                (throw (ex-info \"invalid persistent local datom\"\n    62\t                                {:datom d, :entity m})))\n    63\t              d))\n    64\t          (remove (fn [[a _v]] (= a :db/id)) m))))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- pad-datom\n    68\t  \"Pad [e a v] / [e a v t m] to the canonical 5-tuple. The transactor owns\n    69\t   transaction time: a non-nil explicit t is rejected, a nil t is stamped\n    70\t   with the allocated `t`. A nil m takes the default assertion op; an\n    71\t   explicit m (0, a retraction) is preserved.\"\n    72\t  [d t]\n    73\t  (let [[e a v dt dm] d]\n    74\t    (when-not (nil? dt)\n    75\t      (throw\n    76\t        (ex-info\n    77\t          \"the transactor owns transaction time: explicit datom t is rejected\"\n    78\t          {:datom d})))\n    79\t    (let [padded [e a v t (if (nil? dm) datom/default-op dm)]]\n    80\t      (when-not (datom/local-datom? padded)\n    81\t        (throw (ex-info \"invalid persistent local datom\"\n    82\t                        {:datom padded, :input d})))\n    83\t      padded)))\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\t(defn- val->datoms\n    87\t  [val t]\n    88\t  (cond\n    89\t    (map? val) (entity->datoms val t)\n    90\t    (and (vector? val) (<= 3 (count val) 5)) [(pad-datom val t)]\n    91\t    :else\n    92\t    (throw\n    93\t      (ex-info\n    94\t        \"a value must be an entity map or datom vector [e a v] / [e a v nil m]\"\n    95\t        {:val val}))))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(defn- with-write-lock\n   102\t  \"Serialize timestamp allocation and append on hosts with shared-memory\n   103\t   threads. ClojureScript and ClojureDart calls are synchronous within one\n   104\t   isolate, so the direct call has the same single-writer semantics.\"\n   105\t  [lock f]\n   106\t  #?(:clj (locking lock (f))\n   107\t     :default (f)))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn- append-packet!\n   111\t  \"Append one atomic transaction record to the local stream. The watermark\n   112\t   advances only after the underlying ds/append! answers {:result :ok}; on\n   113\t   any other result or on a thrown error the wrapper keeps the same t and\n   114\t   the call can be retried. Returns {:result :ok, :t t, :datoms datoms}.\"\n   115\t  [local-stream next-t t datoms context]\n   116\t  (let [record {:dao.space/transaction {:t t, :datoms datoms}}\n   117\t        result (ds/append! local-stream record)]\n   118\t    (when-not (and (map? result) (= :ok (:result result)))\n   119\t      (throw (ex-info (str context \" stream append failed: \" (pr-str result))\n   120\t                      {:result result, :t t, :datoms datoms})))\n   121\t    (swap! next-t inc)\n   122\t    {:result :ok, :t t, :datoms datoms}))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn- derive-next-t\n   126\t  \"Derive the next transaction time from a flattened retained history: 0 for\n   127\t   an empty history, else 1 + the maximum datom t. A datom t that is not a\n   128\t   non-negative integer is a malformed history and throws — this scan is the\n   129\t   causality boundary of the wrapper.\"\n   130\t  [datoms]\n   131\t  (if (empty? datoms)\n   132\t    0\n   133\t    (let [ts (mapv index/datom-t datoms)]\n   134\t      (when-not (every? #(and (integer? %) (<= 0 %)) ts)\n   135\t        (throw\n   136\t          (ex-info\n   137\t            \"malformed retained history: datom t must be a non-negative integer\"\n   138\t            {:history datoms})))\n   139\t      (inc (reduce max ts)))))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(deftype DaoStreamLog\n   143\t  [local-stream intake-pool stream-name next-t state]\n   144\t\n   145\t  ds/IDaoStreamWriter\n   146\t\n   147\t  (append!\n   148\t    [_this val]\n   149\t    (with-write-lock\n   150\t      next-t\n   151\t      (fn []\n   152\t        (when (:closed @state)\n   153\t          (throw (ex-info \"Cannot append to closed stream\"\n   154\t                          {:name stream-name})))\n   155\t        (let [t @next-t\n   156\t              datoms (val->datoms val t)]\n   157\t          (when (empty? datoms)\n   158\t            (throw (ex-info \"append! produced no datoms\" {:val val})))\n   159\t          (append-packet! local-stream next-t t datoms \"append!\")))))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t  ds/IDaoStreamReader\n   163\t\n   164\t  (next [_this cursor] (ds/next local-stream cursor))\n   165\t\n   166\t\n   167\t  ds/IDaoStreamBound\n   168\t\n   169\t  (close!\n   170\t    [_this]\n   171\t    (with-write-lock next-t\n   172\t      (fn [] (swap! state assoc :closed true) {:woke []})))\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\t  (closed? [_this] (:closed @state)))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t(ds/defopen\n   179\t  :transactor\n   180\t  [descriptor]\n   181\t  (let [{:keys [local-stream intake-pool name]} descriptor\n   182\t        stream-name (or name \"transactor\")]\n   183\t    (when (contains? descriptor :next-t)\n   184\t      (throw\n   185\t        (ex-info\n   186\t          \":transactor derives transaction time from retained history; :next-t is not accepted\"\n   187\t          {:descriptor descriptor})))\n   188\t    (when-not (and (satisfies? ds/IDaoStreamReader local-stream)\n   189\t                   (satisfies? ds/IDaoStreamWriter local-stream))\n   190\t      (throw\n   191\t        (ex-info\n   192\t          \":transactor descriptor requires a :local-stream satisfying IDaoStreamReader and IDaoStreamWriter\"\n   193\t          {:descriptor descriptor})))\n   194\t    (when-not (and (coll? intake-pool) (seq intake-pool))\n   195\t      (throw\n   196\t        (ex-info\n   197\t          \":transactor descriptor requires a non-empty :intake-pool of streams satisfying the dao.stream writer surface\"\n   198\t          {:descriptor descriptor})))\n   199\t    (doseq [intake intake-pool]\n   200\t      (when-not (stream/writer? intake)\n   201\t        (throw\n   202\t          (ex-info\n   203\t            \":transactor :intake-pool members must satisfy IDaoStreamWriter\"\n   204\t            {:intake-pool intake-pool}))))\n   205\t    (let [next-t (derive-next-t (index/snapshot-datoms local-stream))]\n   206\t      (->DaoStreamLog local-stream\n   207\t                      intake-pool\n   208\t                      stream-name\n   209\t                      (atom next-t)\n   210\t                      (atom {:closed false})))))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn publish!\n   214\t  \"Build and enqueue the covered indexes over the local stream into the\n   215\t   intake pool (dao.space.index/publish-index!), returning its\n   216\t   {:manifest-address ... :manifest ...}. opts are passed through to\n   217\t   publish-index! (e.g. :branching-factor, :select-stream). Publication is\n   218\t   explicit and acknowledges enqueuing only, never observer\n   219\t   materialization.\"\n   220\t  ([log] (publish! log nil))\n   221\t  ([^DaoStreamLog log opts]\n   222\t   (index/publish-index! (.-local-stream log) (.-intake-pool log) opts)))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\t(defn transact!\n   226\t  \"Commits a non-empty collection of entity maps or datom vectors as a\n   227\t  single atomic transaction: every datom shares one allocated t and lands\n   228\t   in one transaction record through exactly one ds/append!, so no partial\n   229\t   prefix is possible. Throws when the stream is closed, the collection is\n   230\t   empty, any item is invalid, or the expansion yields no datoms.\"\n   231\t  [^DaoStreamLog log tx-data]\n   232\t  (when (empty? tx-data)\n   233\t    (throw (ex-info \"transact! requires at least one transaction item\"\n   234\t                    {:tx-data tx-data})))\n   235\t  (let [next-t (.-next-t log)]\n   236\t    (with-write-lock\n   237\t      next-t\n   238\t      (fn []\n   239\t        (when (ds/closed? log)\n   240\t          (throw (ex-info \"Cannot transact! to closed stream\"\n   241\t                          {:name (.-stream-name log)})))\n   242\t        (let [t @next-t\n   243\t              datoms (into [] (mapcat #(val->datoms % t)) tx-data)]\n   244\t          (when (empty? datoms)\n   245\t            (throw (ex-info \"transact! produced no datoms\" {:tx-data tx-data})))\n   246\t          (append-packet! (.-local-stream log) next-t t datoms \"transact!\"))))))\ntest/agent/tzu_test.cljc:180:             (let [next-result (ds/next s {:position 0})]\ntest/agent/tools_test.cljc:30:         (let [next-result (ds/next s {:position 0})]\nsrc/cljc/agent/tools.cljc:125:              result (ds/next stream {:position pos})]\nsrc/cljc/agent/tools.cljc:174:                               (let [res (ds/next s {:position pos})]\nsrc/cljs/yin/vm/telemetry_viewer.cljs:133:              (let [result (ds/next (:tel-stream @app-state) cursor)]\nsrc/cljs/datomworld/ws_client_demo.cljs:20:      (let [result (ds/next stream cursor)]\ntest/dao/postgraphics/terminal_test.cljc:38:    (let [signal (:ok (ds/next signals {:position 0}))]\ntest/dao/postgraphics/terminal_test.cljc:58:           (:ok (ds/next signals {:position 1}))))))\ntest/dao/postgraphics/terminal_test.cljc:72:    (let [signal (:ok (ds/next signals {:position 0}))]\ntest/dao/postgraphics/terminal_test.cljc:76:           (:ok (ds/next signals {:position 1}))))\ntest/dao/postgraphics/terminal_test.cljc:77:    (is (= :blocked (ds/next signals {:position 2})))))\ntest/dao/await_test.cljc:62:            {:keys [ok]} (ds/next out c)]\ntest/dao/await_test.cljc:81:      (let [{:keys [ok]} (ds/next out {:position 0})] (is (= 11 ok))))))\ntest/dao/stream_test.cljc:61:      (is (= :daostream/gap (ds/next stream {:position 2})))\ntest/dao/stream_test.cljc:62:      (is (= :blocked (ds/next stream {:position 3})))\ntest/dao/stream_test.cljc:65:             (ds/next stream {:position 3}))))))\ntest/dao/stream_test.cljc:85:          r1 (ds/next s {:position 0})]\ntest/dao/stream_test.cljc:89:      (let [r2 (ds/next s (:cursor r1))]\ntest/dao/stream_test.cljc:93:    (let [s (make-stream)] (is (= :blocked (ds/next s {:position 0})))))\ntest/d