ljc:173:  [request-handle request-cursor]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:174:  (stream/next request-handle request-cursor))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:178:  \"Read one raw response value at the explicit cursor.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:179:  [response-handle response-cursor]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:180:  (stream/next response-handle response-cursor))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:218:  \"Create caller-owned state for `serve-once!`.  The cursor must have been\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:220:  [request-cursor]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:221:  {:request-cursor request-cursor\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:261:                       (assoc :request-cursor (:pending-successor state))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:272:      ;; this binding.  Retrying would rerun neither handler nor cursor, but\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:277:                       (assoc :request-cursor (:pending-successor state)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:287:                       (assoc :request-cursor (:pending-successor state)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:305:   successor cursor remain in that state until append succeeds, so retrying on\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:317:    (let [read-result (next-request request-handle (:request-cursor state))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:322:              successor (:dao.stream/cursor read-result)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:330:                             (assoc :request-cursor successor)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:341:        :dao.stream/gap\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:342:        (step-result :dao.stream.apply/gap\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:344:                         (assoc :request-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor read-result))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:347:                                  :dao.stream.apply/request-gap}))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc:350:        (:dao.stream/end :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch :dao.stream/invalid-cursor\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:58:       (= :evict-oldest (:retention x))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:356:                     (some? (:ack-cursor slot)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:469:   self-scheduling.  Returns the endpoint after retaining its next cursors.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:482:    (let [next (stream/next (:dao.stream/handle (:ack slot)) (:ack-cursor slot))]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:484:        (swap! (:state endpoint) assoc-in [:slots index :ack-cursor] (:dao.stream/cursor next))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '1,220p'\nnl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '220,480p'\nnl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '480,652p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '1,220p'\nnl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '220,480p'\nnl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '480,652p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-08 14:24 GMT\n     2\tCompleted-Local: 2026-09-08 21:24 +0700 (Asia/Bangkok)\n     3\tCoding-Agent: claude (Opus 5)\n     4\tSession-ID: 6378e1b0-1c5d-4e10-8ea0-61551c03c828\n     5\t\n     6\t# Plan: dao.space.transactor and dao.space.index → dao.stream (r2)\n     7\t\n     8\t## Context\n     9\t\n    10\t`dao.space.transactor` is the seam between v1 and v2: it validates its intake\n    11\tpool with v2 `stream/writer?` but requires its local stream to satisfy the v1\n    12\treader and writer protocols, and it is itself a v1 stream registered through\n    13\t`ds/defopen`. The index plan's D1 established that index cannot close until\n    14\tthis namespace moves, because `publish-index!`'s input *is* the transactor's\n    15\tlocal stream. The owner took that ordering, and then took the index plan's\n    16\tsection 7 as well, so this sweep ends with **both** `dao.space.transactor` and\n    17\t`dao.space.index` free of `dao.stream`, and `dao.space.schema` the only\n    18\t`dao.space` namespace still on v1, under its own plan.\n    19\t\n    20\tMethod: an explicit invariants list is the contract, marked `[D]` stated in a\n    21\tdesign, `[T]` pinned only by a test, `[T→D]` test-pinned and worth promoting,\n    22\t`[T✗]` an implementation accident dropped with its reason. The existing\n    23\timplementation and tests have no authority beyond the invariants they pin.\n    24\tNothing is in production; tests are re-writable where an invariant is\n    25\tpreserved. Old code is deleted in the phase that replaces it. This plan is\n    26\tdeleted when consumed, so it must leave nothing owed.\n    27\t\n    28\t---\n    29\t\n    30\t## 1. Decisions\n    31\t\n    32\t### D1 — a transactor is not a stream in v2. It is an interpreter over one.\n    33\t\n    34\t`dao.stream.md`'s *Composition* already names this case: \"anything that\n    35\ttransforms one stream into another is an interpreter — it reads via its own\n    36\tcursor and appends to an ordinary output stream — and that lives entirely\n    37\toutside this contract, needing no support from it.\" Take the three v1\n    38\tsurfaces one at a time:\n    39\t\n    40\t- **`append!`** is not a stream append. It takes an entity map or a datom\n    41\t  vector, allocates transaction time, and writes a *transaction record*; it\n    42\t  answers `{:result :ok :t t :datoms datoms}`, a transaction receipt, not a\n    43\t  write outcome. Making that conform to `IDaoStreamWriter` would mean either\n    44\t  lying about the value domain or losing the receipt.\n    45\t- **`next`** (:164) is pure delegation: `(ds/next local-stream cursor)`. The\n    46\t  caller *supplied* the local stream and still holds it, so the delegate adds\n    47\t  nothing but a second name for one sequence. **Nothing outside\n    48\t  `transactor_test` calls it** — `SchemaWrapper` implements only\n    49\t  `ds/IDaoStreamBound`, and `stigmergy_test` reads `(:local agent)` directly.\n    50\t- **`close!`/`closed?`** close nothing. They are a per-handle write gate over\n    51\t  state the wrapper owns.\n    52\t\n    53\tSo the transactor becomes a **plain value with explicit named operations**,\n    54\tthe same move `dao.space.query.md`'s *Bounded realizations are values, not\n    55\tstreams* made for the relation transport and `query/open-published!` made for\n    56\tthe opened index:\n    57\t\n    58\t```clojure\n    59\t(def log (transactor/create! {:local-stream local          ; a v2 handle\n    60\t                              :intake-pool [intake]        ; v2 writers\n    61\t                              :name \"worker-7\"}))          ; optional\n    62\t\n    63\t(transactor/append!   log {:db/id 1 :work/claims \"task\"})\n    64\t(transactor/transact! log [{:db/id 1 :work/claims \"task\"} …])\n    65\t(transactor/publish!  log opts)\n    66\t(transactor/close!    log)\n    67\t;; reads: use `local` — it is the caller's handle and always was\n    68\t```\n    69\t\n    70\t`next` is dropped (T12). `closed?` is dropped (T14): v2 lists a `closed?`\n    71\tpredicate as *Explicitly Absent* because \"a predicate answer is stale the\n    72\tmoment it returns; operation results are authoritative,\" and the replacement\n    73\tis already in the vocabulary — `append!`/`transact!` on a closed transactor\n    74\tanswer `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` as data.\n    75\t\n    76\t### D2 — `ds/defopen :transactor` is replaced by a plain constructor, and the descriptor was never portable.\n    77\t\n    78\tv2 has no registry (*Explicitly Absent*: \"an ambient registry — a\n    79\tnamespace-global dispatch table, or registration as a load-time side effect\").\n    80\tThe replacement is `transactor/create!`, a plain function the caller calls,\n    81\tfollowing `query/open-published!`. The owner did not overrule the name, so it\n    82\tstands.\n    83\t\n    84\t**The descriptor was never a descriptor.** v2's `descriptor` operation is\n    85\t*reachability* data — `valid-descriptor?` requires a portable envelope, and\n    86\tthe whole point is naming a stream across a serialization boundary. The\n    87\t`:transactor` map holds two live handles under `:local-stream` and\n    88\t`:intake-pool`; it could never cross that boundary, so it was a v1 *dispatch*\n    89\trecord wearing the word \"descriptor\". It becomes the constructor's plain\n    90\toptions map. Call it a **spec**, not a descriptor, so the reachability word is\n    91\tnot imported into something that has none. A transactor implements no v2\n    92\tprotocol at all, `IDaoStreamDescriptor` included: it is not on a stream, so it\n    93\thas no identity to project.\n    94\t\n    95\tReturn shape: **the value, or a throw** — not an outcome map. `create!`'s only\n    96\tfailure modes are a malformed spec (a caller bug) and a gap or malformed\n    97\tretained history, and a gap on open is not retryable the way `full` is: the\n    98\tcausality boundary cannot be recovered, and the caller has nothing to do but\n    99\tabort. This is the layering index already settled — the snapshot mechanism is\n   100\ttotal and returns every stopping outcome as data; *throwing is the policy of\n   101\tthe interpreter above it*. Keeping `create!` aligned with\n   102\t`index/publish-index!` and `query/open-published!` matters more here than\n   103\tsymmetry with the per-write outcomes, which are genuinely retryable.\n   104\t\n   105\t### D3 — operational outcomes become data; argument defects keep throwing.\n   106\t\n   107\t`append-packet!` (:110-122) throws when the local append answers anything but\n   108\t`{:result :ok}`. In v2 the local append answers `ok | full | invalid-value |\n   109\tclosed | transport-error`, and **`full` means \"not yet, retry\"** — throwing on\n   110\tit was always wrong, because it converts a normal backpressure signal into an\n   111\texception the caller must catch to obey the retry contract the docstring\n   112\talready promises.\n   113\t\n   114\t| Case | v1 | v2 |\n   115\t|---|---|---|\n   116\t| local append ok | `{:result :ok :t t :datoms ds}`, watermark advances | `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.space/t t :dao.space/datoms ds}`, watermark advances |\n   117\t| local append `full`/`closed`/`invalid-value`/`transport-error` | throws | returned as data, watermark **unchanged**, same `t` still pending |\n   118\t| local append answers a non-outcome | throws | folded to `:dao.stream/transport-error` with `:dao.stream/answer` retained |\n   119\t| transactor itself closed | throws | `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` |\n   120\t| malformed entity map / explicit datom `t` / empty `tx-data` / zero datoms | throws | **still throws** |\n   121\t| local append throws | propagates, watermark unchanged | unchanged |\n   122\t\n   123\tThe last row of throws stays because those are defects in the caller's own\n   124\targument, detected before any stream is touched — they are the transactor's\n   125\tcontract with its caller, not the stream's outcome algebra, and converting\n   126\tthem is a behaviour change this migration does not force.\n   127\t`:dao.stream/invalid-value` is available if the owner later wants them as\n   128\tdata; say so in the design and leave it.\n   129\t\n   130\t**The retry contract gets stronger, not weaker.** It was prose plus a throw;\n   131\tit becomes checkable: *the watermark advances if and only if the local append\n   132\tanswered `:dao.stream/ok`*, so retrying the identical call re-attempts the\n   133\tidentical `t`.\n   134\t\n   135\tValidate the local stream's answer with `stream/valid-outcome?` before\n   136\tbranching, exactly as `observe/valid-or-transport-error` does. That helper is\n   137\tprivate to `observe`; a four-line local copy is the right call rather than\n   138\twidening `observe`'s surface for one caller — note the duplication in the\n   139\tdocstring so a third copy triggers promotion instead of accumulating.\n   140\t\n   141\t### D4 — `derive-next-t` keeps its O(history) replay.\n   142\t\n   143\tKeep, unchanged, and record the cost rather than paying for it here.\n   144\t\n   145\tThe local stream is the **only durable truth**. The watermark is derived\n   146\tstate, so it must be recoverable from that truth; any stored counter is a\n   147\tsecond durable truth that can disagree with the first, and reconciling two\n   148\ttruths is a design, not an optimization. It is also not a new cost — the scan\n   149\tis the same walk `publish-index!` already performs on every publish, and\n   150\t`dao.space.index.md` already states that full retention is required for\n   151\texactly this reason.\n   152\t\n   153\tNote in *Open items* that the eventual relief keeps one truth (the log carries\n   154\tits own checkpoint) rather than adding a second. Do not design it here.\n   155\t\n   156\t### D5 — the shared mechanism is `dao.stream.observe/snapshot`. No `drain`.\n   157\t\n   158\tTaking the owner's naming rule as given: the destructive-read vocabulary stays\n   159\tout of the namespace named for observation. Once the local stream is v2, there\n   160\tare genuinely two consumers of one loop — mint at `:dao.stream/oldest`, run\n   161\t`observe/step` with a *total* effect that retains the value and answers `ok`,\n   162\tstop when the step stops — so promote it, keeping the name:\n   163\t\n   164\t```clojure\n   165\t(observe/snapshot handle)\n   166\t;; => {:values   [v …]\n   167\t;;     :status   :ended | :blocked | :gap | :defect\n   168\t;;     :cursor   c           ; the cursor reached; on :gap the last retained\n   169\t;;     :recovery c'          ; :gap only\n   170\t;;     :read     raw}        ; :defect only\n   171\t```\n   172\t\n   173\tIt returns **`:values`** — not a relation (that is query's tag) and not datoms\n   174\t(that is index's vocabulary). It carries no policy: every stopping outcome is\n   175\tdata, and the cursor never advances past a value the accumulator did not\n   176\tretain, which is `step`'s effect-before-commit and comes for free.\n   177\t\n   178\tEach caller keeps its own policy, and the two only ever *looked* like they\n   179\tdisagreed:\n   180\t\n   181\t- `query/snapshot` = `observe/snapshot` + `(relation values)`, statuses passed\n   182\t  through, because a partial relation may still be a usable query input.\n   183\t- `index/snapshot-datoms` = `observe/snapshot` + throw on `:gap`/`:defect` +\n   184\t  `datoms-from-elements`, because `publish-index!` must abort before emitting\n   185\t  anything (`dao.space.index.md`: \"a retention gap aborts publication before\n   186\t  anything is emitted\").\n   187\t\n   188\t`observe`'s ns docstring says `step` \"owns no scheduler, loop, state, callback\n   189\tor policy\" and that callers add their own loop. Amend it: the namespace holds\n   190\t`step` plus the one total-effect loop that has more than one consumer, and\n   191\t`snapshot` inherits the no-policy rule verbatim — it *has* a loop, it still\n   192\thas no policy.\n   193\t\n   194\t### D6 — schema moves at its call sites only, and does not need its own migration to do it.\n   195\t\n   196\t`SchemaWrapper` implements only `ds/IDaoStreamBound`, and both methods\n   197\tdelegate to the transactor handle. When the transactor drops `closed?`, schema\n   198\tholds the flag itself — it already has a per-wrapper `state` atom for exactly\n   199\tthis kind of coordination, so `close!` sets `:closed` and calls `tx/close!`,\n   200\tand `closed?` reads it. That is three lines, not a migration.\n   201\t\n   202\tWhat Phase 3 forces in schema, and nothing more:\n   203\t\n   204\t| schema site | forced edit |\n   205\t|---|---|\n   206\t| `:965` `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor …}` | → `tx/create!` |\n   207\t| `:949` `close!` → `(ds/close! inner)` | → set own `:closed`, call `tx/close!` |\n   208\t| `:954` `closed?` → `(ds/closed? inner)` | → read own `:closed` |\n   209\t| `:1112` `(tx/transact! (.-inner wrapper) datoms)` and `schema/transact!`'s own return | receipt shape follows D3 |\n   210\t| `:926`, `:969` `index/snapshot-datoms local-stream` | code unchanged; the handle they receive is now v2 |\n   211\t| `schema/transactor`'s `local-stream` argument | callers pass a v2 handle |\n   212\t\n   213\t`(.-inner wrapper)` keeps working: the field just holds a map now. Phase 5\n   214\tadds exactly one more schema edit, bounded in section 7.\n   215\t\n   216\t### D7 — index ends this sweep requiring no `dao.stream` (restated)\n   217\t\n   218\tThe r1 version of this decision said index keeps `[dao.stream :as ds]` for the\n   219\tpublished adapter. With Phase 5 that is false. Verified against the tree\n   220\trather than assumed — every `ds/` occurrence in `src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc`:\n   220\trather than assumed — every `ds/` occurrence in `src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc`:\n   221\t\n   222\t| line | use | closed by |\n   223\t|---|---|---|\n   224\t| :347 | `ds/IDaoStreamReader` (PublishedIndexStream impl) | Phase 5 |\n   225\t| :358 | `ds/IDaoStreamBound` (PublishedIndexStream impl) | Phase 5 |\n   226\t| :383 | `ds/defopen :dao.space.index/published` | Phase 5 |\n   227\t| :444 | the string \"ds/next\" inside `snapshot-datoms`' docstring | Phase 3 |\n   228\t| :453 | `(ds/next local-stream cursor)` | Phase 3 |\n   229\t\n   230\tThat is the complete list — five occurrences, of which one is prose. The\n   231\towner's measurement (`snapshot-datoms` :451-468 and the published adapter\n   232\t:344-404 as the only two regions) is confirmed. There is no\n   233\t`#?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream]))` in `index.cljc` to remove; its `ns`\n   234\tform ends at :41.\n   235\t\n   236\t**At the end of Phase 5, `dao.space.index` requires exactly:**\n   237\t`dao.data.btree`, `dao.data.btree.storage`, `dao.datom`, `dao.jing`,\n   238\t`dao.jing.coordinate`, `dao.stream`, and `dao.stream.observe` (new in\n   239\tPhase 3). `dao.jing.coordinate` survives only if something in index still\n   240\topens a coordinate — after Phase 5 it does not, since `published-index` merely\n   241\t*constructs* the coordinate map, so **`dao.jing.coordinate` goes too**. The\n   242\timplementer must confirm this at the end of Phase 5 rather than trusting the\n   243\tlist: `grep -n \"jing-coordinate/\\|ds/\" src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc` must\n   244\treturn nothing.\n   245\t\n   246\t`test/dao/space/index_test.cljc` likewise ends with zero `ds/` uses and drops\n   247\tits `[dao.stream :as ds]` require — see Phase 5 for the accounting of all 41\n   248\tcurrent occurrences.\n   249\t\n   250\t---\n   251\t\n   252\t## 2. The invariants this plan is accountable to\n   253\t\n   254\t### Transactor\n   255\t\n   256\t| # | Invariant | |\n   257\t|---|---|---|\n   258\t| T1 | Every `append!`/`transact!` writes exactly ONE atomic transaction record `{:dao.space/transaction {:t n :datoms […]}}` through exactly one local append, so no reader observes a torn transaction | `[D]` |\n   259\t| T2 | `t` comes from a per-wrapper watermark, derived on open as 0 for empty history else 1 + max datom `t` | `[D]` |\n   260\t| T3 | A caller-supplied `:next-t` is rejected | `[D]` |\n   261\t| T4 | A retention gap or malformed retained history fails the open | `[D]` |\n   262\t| T5 | The watermark advances **iff** the local append succeeded; a failed or thrown append leaves the same `t` retryable | `[D]` + `[T]` :499, :515 — strengthened by D3 from prose to a returned outcome |\n   263\t| T6 | Single-writer: two wrappers over one local stream derive the same `t` and write colliding records; a documented hazard, not silently coordinated | `[D]` + `[T]` :655 |\n   264\t| T7 | Close is per handle: it rejects further writes and neither closes nor erases the local stream or the intake pool | `[D]` + `[T]` :584 |\n   265\t| T8 | Close linearizes after an in-flight append — no write crosses the point at which close returns | `[T]` :616 → `[T→D]`, it is what \"calls through one wrapper are serialized\" means operationally |\n   266\t| T9 | Opening creates, registers, or closes nothing | `[T]` :273 → `[T→D]`, the \"supplied, never created\" invariant stated from the outside |\n   267\t| T10 | Entity maps require `:db/id`; an explicit datom `t` is rejected; `[e a v]`/`[e a v nil m]` pad to canonical d5 and are validated | `[D]` |\n   268\t| T11 | `publish!` passes the wrapper's local stream, pool and opts to `index/publish-index!` and returns its result; publication acknowledges enqueuing only | `[D]` |\n   269\t| T12 | The wrapper delegates reads | `[T]` :382, :609 → **`[T✗]`**. Pure delegation to a handle the caller supplied and still holds; the only callers are the two tests that pin it. Dropped with `next`. |\n   270\t| T13 | `close!` returns `{:woke []}` | **`[T✗]`**. v2 has no waiter registration (*Explicitly Absent*), so there is no wake list to report. Becomes `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}`. |\n   271\t| T14 | `closed?` is a public predicate | **`[T✗]`**. v2 *Explicitly Absent*, with the stated reason. Replaced by the `:dao.stream/closed` outcome on the next write. |\n   272\t| T15 | An append receipt carries ok, the allocated `t`, and the datoms | `[T]` throughout → preserved, re-spelled in v2 vocabulary: `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.space/t t :dao.space/datoms ds}` |\n   273\t| T16 | Intake pool members are validated with v2 `stream/writer?`; a non-empty collection is required | `[D]`, unchanged |\n   274\t| T17 | A non-ok local append throws | **`[T✗]`**, replaced by D3: returned as data, since `full` is backpressure and the retry contract needs it. |\n   275\t\n   276\t### Index (from the index plan, carried forward)\n   277\t\n   278\t**Snapshot** — S1 reads from cursor zero, full retention required `[D]`; S2\n   279\telement is a canonical d5 vector or a transaction record `[D]`; S3 the\n   280\trecord's exact shape `[T→D]`; S4 `:blocked`/`:end` finish at the tail `[D]`;\n   281\tS5 a gap throws before any emission `[D]`; S6 malformed anything throws before\n   282\tany emission `[D]`; S7 the two distinct diagnostics `[T]`; S8 incremental\n   283\tflattening `[T✗]`, dropped in Phase 1.\n   284\t\n   285\t**Published** — P1 the coordinate's exact shape `[D]`; P2 plain EDN, survives\n   286\ta stream round-trip `[T→D]`; P3 opening fetches exactly one blob, zero nodes\n   287\tfaulted `[D]`; P4 rows deferred, EAVT order, equal to `read-datoms` `[D]`; P5\n   288\ta store opened during a failed open is closed before the error propagates\n   289\t`[D]`; P6 the v1 adapter's reader/bound/not-writer, `closed?`-from-construction\n   290\tand `{:woke []}` close `[T]` — **v1 protocol vocabulary that dies with the\n   291\tadapter in Phase 5**; P7 two independent cursors over one realization `[T✗]`\n   292\t— *Bounded realizations are values, not streams* already ruled that a\n   293\tfully-computed row vector has no second-observer need; P8 `covered-indexes` is\n   294\ta structural check, never an instance check `[D]`.\n   295\t\n   296\t---\n   297\t\n   298\t## 3. Phase 1 — split index's payload vocabulary from its reading\n   299\t\n   300\t`src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc` and its test only; no behaviour change. It\n   301\tlands first because Phase 3 needs the vocabulary separable from the reader.\n   302\t\n   303\t1. Rename private `stream-payload-datoms` → private `element-datoms`. Body\n   304\t   unchanged; S3, S6, S7 preserved verbatim including both error messages.\n   305\t2. Add public `datoms-from-elements`: `(into [] (mapcat element-datoms)\n   306\t   elements)` — the local-stream payload vocabulary, one seq of elements to\n   307\t   canonical local d5 datoms. `into` is eager, so S6's throw-before-emission\n   308\t   ordering is unchanged.\n   309\t3. `snapshot-datoms` becomes drain-then-flatten over the existing v1 loop:\n   310\t   accumulate `(:ok result)` payloads, then `datoms-from-elements` on the\n   311\t   `:blocked`/`:end` exit. Gap and malformed-signal branches unchanged. S8 is\n   312\t   dropped here, with its reason.\n   313\t\n   314\t**Proof.** Add `datoms-from-elements-is-the-local-stream-vocabulary` to\n   315\t`index_test`, pinning S2, S3, S6, S7 directly rather than only through\n   316\t`publish-index!`: a bare datom passes through; a transaction record flattens;\n   317\textra keys / non-integer `:t` / empty `:datoms` / a datom whose `t` disagrees\n   318\twith the record all throw; a 5-vector with a non-namespaced `a` gets\n   319\t\"malformed local datom\"; anything else gets \"must be a datom or dao.space\n   320\ttransaction record\". Every existing snapshot test stays as written and now\n   321\tpins the drain and the composition rather than the vocabulary.\n   322\t\n   323\t## 4. Phase 2 — promote the snapshot loop to `dao.stream.observe/snapshot`\n   324\t\n   325\t1. `src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc`: add `snapshot` per D5. Amend the ns\n   326\t   docstring as D5 describes.\n   327\t2. `src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc`: `snapshot` becomes\n   328\t   `(let [{:keys [values] :as s} (observe/snapshot handle)]\n   329\t      (-> s (dissoc :values) (assoc :relation (relation values))))` — same\n   330\t   public shape, same statuses, loop deleted.\n   331\t3. `test/dao/stream/observe_test.cljc`: move query_test's status-coverage\n   332\t   cases (`snapshot-of-an-open-buffer-is-blocked` :339,\n   333\t   `snapshot-of-a-closed-buffer-ends` :350, `snapshot-of-a-gap-is-data` :359,\n   334\t   `snapshot-of-a-defect-carries-the-raw-answer` :386,\n   335\t   `snapshot-never-closes-the-handle` :402) down to `observe/snapshot`, where\n   336\t   they now belong, restating them over `:values`. `query_test` keeps\n   337\t   `snapshot-relation-feeds-current-and-q` (:410), which is the relation\n   338\t   wrapper's own property.\n   339\t\n   340\tThe second consumer arrives in Phase 3 of *this* plan, so this promotion is\n   341\tsequencing rather than speculation. Stated plainly because it is the one place\n   342\tthe index plan's rule (\"promote when the second consumer appears\") runs a\n   343\tphase early: if Phase 3 were abandoned, Phase 2 should be reverted with it.\n   344\t\n   345\t## 5. Phase 3 — the swap\n   346\t\n   347\tOne phase, because the constraint forbids leaving the `defopen` and\n   348\t`DaoStreamLog` half-deleted and every consumer breaks at the same instant.\n   349\t\n   350\t**`src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc`** — delete `DaoStreamLog` and\n   351\t`ds/defopen :transactor`; delete the `[dao.stream :as ds]` require and the\n   352\t`#?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream]))`.\n   353\t\n   354\t- `create!` per D2: validate the spec (reject `:next-t`; require a\n   355\t  `stream/reader?`-and-`stream/writer?` local stream; require a non-empty pool\n   356\t  of `stream/writer?` members — the pool check at :199-204 is already v2 and\n   357\t  moves verbatim), then `(derive-next-t (index/snapshot-datoms local-stream))`\n   358\t  and return `{:dao.space/transactor true :local-stream … :intake-pool …\n   359\t  :name … :next-t (atom t) :state (atom {:closed false})}`. A tag key,\n   360\t  following `:dao.space.query/published`.\n   361\t- `append-packet!` per D3: `stream/append!`, `stream/valid-outcome?`, advance\n   362\t  on `:dao.stream/ok` only, return the local outcome as data otherwise.\n   363\t- `append!` / `transact!` become plain functions over the value, keeping\n   364\t  `with-write-lock`, `val->datoms`, `entity->datoms`, `pad-datom` and\n   365\t  `derive-next-t` exactly as they are. The closed check returns\n   366\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` instead of throwing.\n   367\t- `close!` sets `:closed` inside the write lock and returns\n   368\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}`; idempotent.\n   369\t- `publish!` reads `(:local-stream log)` / `(:intake-pool log)` instead of\n   370\t  deftype fields.\n   371\t- No `next`, no `closed?`.\n   372\t\n   373\t**`src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc`** — `snapshot-datoms` becomes\n   374\t`observe/snapshot` + policy + `datoms-from-elements` per D5; add\n   375\t`[dao.stream.observe :as observe]`. `publish-index!`'s signature is\n   376\tunchanged; its `local-stream` is now a v2 handle. The `ds` require survives\n   377\tthis phase for the published adapter only, and dies in Phase 5.\n   378\t\n   379\t**`src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc`** — the six forced edits in D6's table,\n   380\tnothing else.\n   381\t\n   382\t**Tests.**\n   383\t\n   384\t- `transactor_test`: add `open-local` returning a v2 ringbuffer owner handle;\n   385\t  `open-with-intake` calls `transactor/create!`; the three test doubles\n   386\t  (`FailingAppendStream`, `ThrowingAppendStream`, the `close-linearizes`\n   387\t  `reify`) become v2 writers answering `{:dao.stream/outcome …}`; `tx-ts` and\n   388\t  the atomicity assertions read the local stream through the existing\n   389\t  `intake-values` loop, generalized to `stream-values`.\n   390\t  `readers-observe-atomic-transaction-records` (:382) and the read assertion\n   391\t  at :609 read `local` instead of `log` (T12). Receipt assertions take the D3\n   392\t  shape. `descriptor-validation` becomes `spec-validation`, its throw messages\n   393\t  following the constructor's wording.\n   394\t- `schema_test`, `stigmergy_test:106`, `index_test`'s `open-local`,\n   395\t  `query_test`'s `open-local` (:567), `schema_test:670`: v2 local streams,\n   396\t  under the rule in section 6.\n   397\t\n   398\t**Proof.** The unchanged deftests are the proof: `reopen-derives-next-t-from-\n   399\tretained-history` (:291) for T2, `malformed-or-gapped-retained-history-throws`\n   400\t(:317) for T4, `each-transaction-is-exactly-one-append` (:366) for T1,\n   401\t`append-failure-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry` (:499) and\n   402\t`append-throw-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry` (:515) for T5 — the first now\n   403\tobserving a returned outcome instead of a catch —\n   404\t`close-is-per-handle-and-does-not-touch-local-stream` (:584) for T7 and T13,\n   405\t`close-linearizes-after-an-in-flight-append` (:616) for T8,\n   406\t`single-writer-wrappers-are-not-coordinated` (:655) for T6,\n   407\t`publish-enqueues-indexes-into-the-pool` (:681) for T11. T14's replacement\n   408\tneeds a *new* case: an `append!` and a `transact!` after `close!` each answer\n   409\t`{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` rather than throwing.\n   410\t\n   411\t## 6. The retention-capacity rule\n   412\t\n   413\tThis is the one hazard in the sweep that can pass CI by luck, so it gets its\n   414\town section rather than a note.\n   415\t\n   416\t**The asymmetry.** v1's ring buffer treats a missing capacity as unbounded —\n   417\t`ringbuffer.cljc:82`'s eviction test is `(and capacity …)`, so\n   418\t`{:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer}` never evicts. v2's `valid-spec?`\n   419\t(`v2/ringbuffer.cljc:15-20`) *requires* a positive integer capacity and\n   420\t`append!` evicts oldest once the buffer is full. So the migration cannot be\n   421\tmechanical: every unbounded v1 open must acquire a number, and the number is a\n   422\tcorrectness decision, not a formality.\n   423\t\n   424\t**Why the transactor is the worst possible place for it.** `derive-next-t` and\n   425\t`publish-index!` both read from position zero and both require complete\n   426\tretained history. An undersized capacity does not fail to compile and does not\n   427\tfail at the append that overflows — it fails later, at the *next* `create!` or\n   428\t`publish!`, as a `:dao.stream/gap`. Left undersized in a test that never\n   429\treopens or republishes, it fails nowhere at all, and the plan would have\n   430\tquietly traded a causality invariant for a green suite.\n   431\t\n   432\t**Measured scope.** There are **29** exact `{:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer}`\n   433\topens (no capacity) across `src` and `test`, one more than the owner's 28, and\n   434\tthe more useful fact is where they are: **all 29 are in `dao.space` tests** —\n   435\t`transactor_test` 22, `index_test` 2, `schema_test` 2, `query_test` 2,\n   436\t`stigmergy_test` 1. No `src` namespace opens an unbounded ring buffer. The\n   437\thazard is entirely inside the files this plan already touches.\n   438\t\n   439\t**Three of the 29 must not be migrated**, and mistaking them for the others is\n   440\tits own defect:\n   441\t\n   442\t| site | why it stays v1 |\n   443\t|---|---|\n   444\t| `query_test:97` | not an open at all — a literal map passed to `q` to prove a raw map is rejected as a db input |\n   445\t| `schema_test:304` | builds a *closed v1 realization* for `schema/current`'s borrowed-input path; that is schema's own v1 surface, under schema's plan |\n   446\t| `index_test:777` | the descriptor carrier, deleted outright in Phase 5 |\n   447\t\n   448\tThe remaining **26** migrate.\n   449\t\n   450\t**The rule the implementer follows at every one of the 26.** Do not pick a\n   451\tcapacity per call site. Define exactly one named constant per test namespace —\n   452\t`local-capacity`, at 65536 — use it for every migrated local stream, and never\n   453\tinline a literal. Then:\n   454\t\n   455\t1. If a site's history is bounded by the test's own appends, the constant is\n   456\t   correct by inspection and the review is one comparison, not 26.\n   457\t2. If a site *deliberately* wants eviction, it takes an explicit small\n   458\t   capacity and a comment saying which gap it is provoking. There is exactly\n   459\t   one such site today, `index_test:379`, which already passes a capacity and\n   460\t   therefore is not in the 26.\n   461\t\n   462\t**How a violation is caught rather than passing by luck.** A too-small\n   463\tcapacity is only observable through a *second* read from position zero, so add\n   464\tone test that forces exactly that, in `transactor_test`:\n   465\t\n   466\t> `retained-history-survives-reopen-at-capacity` — append more transaction\n   467\t> records than a deliberately small capacity retains, then `create!` a second\n   468\t> transactor over the same local stream and assert it throws the retention-gap\n   469\t> error (T4). Then repeat at `local-capacity` and assert the reopen succeeds\n   470\t> and derives the expected `t`.\n   471\t\n   472\tThat test fails loudly if the constant is ever lowered below what the suite\n   473\tappends, and it pins T4 against a real eviction rather than the synthetic gap\n   474\tstream `index_test:379` uses. Without it, `derive-next-t`'s dependence on full\n   475\tretention is pinned only by a hand-built gap, which is exactly the kind of\n   476\tcoverage that survives a capacity regression.\n   477\t\n   478\t## 7. Phase 4 — documentation for the transactor migration\n   479\t\n   480\t- **`docs/design/dao.space.index.md`**: *The agent-transactor loop* — replace\n   480\t- **`docs/design/dao.space.index.md`**: *The agent-transactor loop* — replace\n   481\t  the `ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor …}` sample (:195-210) and the\n   482\t  descriptor sentence (:191) with `transactor/create!` and the spec; add\n   483\t  `datoms-from-elements` to the public surface; restate *The snapshot* as\n   484\t  vocabulary + `observe/snapshot`.\n   485\t- **`docs/design/dao.space.md`**: *The Write Path* sample at :509 and the\n   486\t  descriptor mention at :476.\n   487\t- **`docs/design/dao.space.schema.md`**: :247 and :383 — the wrapper wraps a\n   488\t  transactor *value* and owns its own closedness.\n   489\t- **`docs/design/dao.space.query.md`**: *Snapshots* — the mechanism is now\n   490\t  `observe/snapshot`; `query/snapshot` is its relation-tagging caller; the gap\n   491\t  policy stays with each caller.\n   492\t- **`docs/design/dao.stream.md`**: *The v2 namespace is transient* — drop\n   493\t  `transactor` from the remaining-consumer list. Phase 5 drops `index`.\n   494\t- A new `dao.space.transactor` section (or its own doc, owner's call) carrying\n   495\t  T1–T11, T15, T16, D3's outcome table, the retention-capacity rule from\n   496\t  section 6, and D4's O(history) note as an Open item.\n   497\t\n   498\tPhases 4 and 5 are order-independent; Phase 5 carries its own doc edits, so\n   499\tevery phase ends with the docs true.\n   500\t\n   501\t## 8. Phase 5 — index closes\n   502\t\n   503\t**What is built.** One rewritten `defopen` body in `dao.space.schema`:\n   504\t\n   505\t```clojure\n   506\t(ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/published\n   507\t  [descriptor]\n   508\t  ;; validate exactly as today, then:\n   509\t  (let [store (jing-coordinate/open! content-store)\n   510\t        rows  (try (index/read-datoms store manifest-address)\n   511\t                   (finally (jing/close! store)))]\n   512\t    (->PublishedSchemaRows rows)))\n   513\t```\n   514\t\n   515\t`PublishedSchemaRows` is a small private record in `schema.cljc` implementing\n   516\t`ds/IDaoStreamReader` (`next` by position over the vector) and\n   517\t`ds/IDaoStreamBound` (`close!` → `{:woke []}`, `closed?` → true). This is\n   518\t*simpler* than what it replaces: schema forces the whole row vector at open\n   519\tanyway (`ds/strict-vec` at :1167), so nothing on this path ever needed the\n   520\tlazy restored trees or a retained store handle. The store is closed inside the\n   521\topener instead of surviving until `schema/current` closes the reader, which\n   522\talso removes the comment at :1163-1166 explaining why the delay had to be\n   523\tforced before the store went away.\n   524\t\n   525\t**What is deleted.**\n   526\t- `schema.cljc:1161` `ds/open! (index/published-index …)` and `:1167`\n   527\t  `ds/strict-vec` — replaced by the body above.\n   528\t- `index.cljc:344-363` `PublishedIndexStream`.\n   529\t- `index.cljc:383-404` `ds/defopen :dao.space.index/published`.\n   530\t- `index.cljc`'s `[dao.stream :as ds]` and `[dao.jing.coordinate :as\n   531\t  jing-coordinate]` requires (D7).\n   532\t- `index_test`'s `[dao.stream :as ds]` require, after the accounting below.\n   533\t\n   534\t**What Phase 5 must not touch.** The edit is one `defopen` body. Explicitly\n   535\tout of bounds:\n   536\t- `ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/current` (:357) and its whole opener —\n   537\t  untouched.\n   538\t- `SchemaWrapper` (:943-955) beyond the three closedness edits Phase 3 already\n   539\t  forces.\n   540\t- `ds/strict-vec` at :260 and `ds/realization?` at :259/:318 — the\n   541\t  borrowed-input path, schema's own surface.\n   542\t- `schema_test:304`'s v1 realization fixture.\n   543\t- Schema's closedness model beyond D6's table.\n   544\t\n   545\t**The ten `ds/open!` adapter call sites, per test.** They are ten call sites\n   546\tacross eight deftests. Each property is accounted for, because a deleted test\n   547\twhose property is not covered elsewhere is a defect:\n   548\t\n   549\t| # | `index_test` deftest (line, `ds/open!` sites) | property | disposition |\n   550\t|---|---|---|---|\n   551\t| 1 | `open-published-rejects-unresolvable-and-malformed-descriptors` (:586; 600, 611) | an unsupported coordinate type fails closed at open; an extra key is rejected — P1 | **Moved, not deleted.** Rewrite onto `query/open-published!` in `query_test`. Nothing there covers coordinate rejection today, so deleting outright would drop P1's open-time half. |\n   552\t| 2 | `open-published-rejects-missing-and-invalid-manifests` (:624; 637, 647) | a missing manifest address throws; a stored non-manifest throws | **Deleted.** Covered by `read-manifest-guards-missing-and-invalid` (:823), which pins both throws directly on `read-manifest`/`read-datoms` — the functions the new opener and `open-published!` both call. |\n   553\t| 3 | `published-realization-is-read-only-with-a-stable-lifecycle` (:651; 656) | reader+bound not writer, `closed?` from construction, `{:woke []}` idempotent close, close does not erase — P6; EAVT order; two independent cursors — P7 | **Deleted.** P6 is v1 protocol vocabulary that dies with the adapter; P7 is dropped per the index plan. EAVT order survives in #7's replacement and in `read-datoms`' own tests; idempotent close survives as `close-published-closes-once-and-is-idempotent` (`query_test`:715). |\n   554\t| 4 | `published-empty-index-drains-to-end` (:681; 683) | an empty manifest reads as no datoms, not an error | **Deleted, with one addition.** `publish-index-of-empty-input-is-readable` (:351) already covers it through `read-datoms`; add one `query_test` case that `open-published!` on an empty manifest yields an empty relation, since the *opened* path is otherwise uncovered. |\n   555\t| 5 | `published-open-fetches-only-the-manifest` (:690; 700) | exactly one content fetch at open, zero nodes faulted — P3 | **Moved, not deleted.** `lazy-published-node-budget-is-strictly-bounded` (`query_test`:737) bounds *total* gets after a query at ≤ 4; it does not pin the open-time count. Add `open-published-fetches-only-the-manifest` to `query_test` asserting exactly 1 get after `open-published!` and before any read, reusing the existing `counting-content-store` helper. |\n   556\t| 6 | `covered-indexes-returns-the-four-covered-sets` (:708; 710) | the opened realization carries the four sets; the check is structural, never an instance check — P8 | **Kept, minus the open.** The structural cases (nil, `{}`, wrong key sets, a plain four-key map) need no opened value and stay verbatim. The \"an opened realization carries the four sets\" case moves onto `query/open-published!`'s value, which carries `:indexes` — and that move is itself the proof of P8, since a plain map and an opened index are indistinguishable to `covered-indexes`. |\n   557\t| 7 | `published-next-yields-the-same-eavt-rows-as-the-eager-walk` (:736; 741) | the deferred rows equal the eager walk, in EAVT order — P4 | **Moved.** Rewrite in `query_test` as `open-published!`'s forced `:rows` delay versus `index/read-datoms`. |\n   558\t| 8 | `published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream` (:759; 783, plus the carrier at 777) | the coordinate is plain EDN, exact-bounded, carries the EAVT comparator, travels through a stream, and opens on the far side — P2 | **Moved and modernized.** Keep the `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip and the carrier — now a **v2** ring buffer — and open the transported coordinate with `query/open-published!`. `ds/exact-bound?` (:779) is v1; replace it with a direct assertion on `{:manifest-address …}`, which is what P1 fixes anyway. |\n   559\t\n   560\t**`index_test`'s remaining 41 `ds/` occurrences.** After Phase 3 migrates\n   561\t`open-local` (:69) and the gap fixture (:382), `stream-values` (:122), and the\n   562\tmalformed-signal reader double (:27-30) to v2, and Phase 5 removes the eight\n   563\tdeftests above, the residue is zero. The implementer confirms with `grep -c\n   564\t\"ds/\" test/dao/space/index_test.cljc` returning 0 and drops the require; a\n   565\tnon-zero count means a property was migrated by hand instead of by rule.\n   566\t\n   567\t**Proof for Phase 5.** `stigmergy_test` is the end-to-end check that the new\n   568\tschema opener is behaviourally identical: it publishes, materializes, and\n   569\tqueries published manifests through `query/open-published!` across both\n   570\t`:dao.jing/file` and `:dao.jing/remote` coordinates. `schema_test` W38–W41\n   571\t(:1449, :1481, :1522) are the direct check on the rewritten opener and must\n   572\tpass **unmodified** — they exercise `schema/published` through\n   573\t`ds/open!`/`schema/current`, which is exactly the surface Phase 5 preserves\n   574\twhile replacing its implementation. If any of the three needs editing, the\n   575\topener's behaviour changed and the phase is wrong.\n   576\t\n   577\t## 9. End condition\n   578\t\n   579\tWhen Phase 5 lands:\n   580\t\n   581\t- **`dao.space.transactor` requires no `dao.stream`.** Its requires are\n   582\t  `dao.datom`, `dao.space.index`, `dao.stream`.\n   583\t- **`dao.space.index` requires no `dao.stream`.** Its requires are\n   584\t  `dao.data.btree`, `dao.data.btree.storage`, `dao.datom`, `dao.jing`,\n   585\t  `dao.stream`, `dao.stream.observe`. Confirmed by grep, not by\n   586\t  inspection (D7).\n   587\t- **`docs/design/dao.stream.md`'s remaining-consumer list drops both**, from\n   588\t  \"`dao.space` (index, schema, transactor — `query` migrated …)\" to\n   589\t  \"`dao.space` (`schema` only — `query`, `index` and `transactor` migrated,\n   590\t  and the `dao.stream.relation` transport was eliminated with `query`)\".\n   591\t- **`dao.space.schema` is the only `dao.space` namespace left on v1.** Its\n   592\t  remaining surface, measured and corrected against the owner's count of \"21\n   593\t  sites across seven APIs\" — the owner's `ds/close! ×4` includes the prose\n   594\t  mention at :1164, so it is 3 call sites, and the protocol references and the\n   595\t  `SchemaWrapper` implementation are three more sites the count folded\n   596\t  together:\n   597\t\n   598\t| API | today | after Phases 3+5 | remaining sites |\n   599\t|---|---|---|---|\n   600\t| `ds/open!` | 4 | 2 | :351, :363 |\n   601\t| `ds/closed?` | 4 | 3 | :323, :1069, :1127 |\n   602\t| `ds/close!` | 3 (+1 in prose) | 2 | :367, :373 |\n   603\t| `ds/strict-vec` | 2 | 1 | :260 |\n   604\t| `ds/realization?` | 2 | 2 | :259, :318 |\n   605\t| `ds/defopen` | 2 | 2 | `:dao.space.schema/current` :357, `:dao.space.schema/published` :1154 (body replaced, form kept) |\n   606\t| `satisfies? ds/IDaoStream*` | 2 | 2 | :319, :364 |\n   607\t| `SchemaWrapper` protocol impl | 1 | 1 | :945 |\n   608\t| **total code sites** | **20** | **15** | |\n   609\t\n   610\t  Plus one *addition*: Phase 5's `PublishedSchemaRows` record. That is\n   611\t  deliberate and worth naming — Phase 5 does not reduce the repo's total v1\n   612\t  surface so much as **relocate index's share of it into the one namespace\n   613\t  that still owes a plan**, where schema's migration deletes the whole\n   614\t  `:dao.space.schema/published` opener and the record with it. A remainder\n   615\t  belongs with its owner.\n   616\t- Nothing in this plan is owed to a later plan except schema's own migration,\n   617\t  which was always its own.\n   618\t\n   619\t## 10. Verification\n   620\t\n   621\tAll three lanes green at the end of **every** phase, plus the demo:\n   622\t\n   623\t```\n   624\tbb test:clj\n   625\tbb test:cljs      # confirm \"Testing dao.space.transactor-test\", \"…index-test\",\n   626\t                  # \"…schema-test\" and \"…observe-test\" appear in the node output\n   627\tbb test:cljd\n   628\tclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n   629\t```\n   630\t\n   631\t- **Demo.** `datomworld.demo` requires only `datomworld.demo.*`, `reagent` and\n   632\t  `yin.vm.telemetry-viewer` — it reaches no `dao.space` namespace — so a break\n   633\t  would be a compile regression rather than a behavioural one. Compile it each\n   634\t  phase anyway, as the constraint requires.\n   635\t- **Phase 3 is the likeliest red**, and the two failure shapes are (a) an\n   636\t  undersized ring-buffer capacity surfacing as\n   637\t  `malformed-or-gapped-retained-history-throws` (:317) or a publish gap, and\n   638\t  (b) a receipt-shape assertion missed in the ~30 migrated sites. Section 6's\n   639\t  new `retained-history-survives-reopen-at-capacity` exists so (a) is loud\n   640\t  rather than latent.\n   641\t- **`close-linearizes-after-an-in-flight-append` (:616) is the T8 canary**,\n   642\t  JVM-only. If it goes red against the v2 `reify`, the write lock stopped\n   643\t  covering the state transition.\n   644\t- **`schema_test` W38–W41 must pass unmodified through Phase 5** — that is the\n   645\t  phase's own proof, per section 8.\n   646\t- **End-to-end**, `stigmergy_test.clj` covers the whole sweep: agents with v2\n   647\t  local streams, transaction records, publish, observer materialization, and\n   648\t  query over published manifests through both file and remote coordinates. If\n   649\t  it passes, T1, T2, T11, S1–S6 and P1–P5 all held across the swap.\n   650\t- **The two greps that close D7**, run at the end of Phase 5, both returning\n   651\t  nothing: `grep -n \"jing-coordinate/\\|ds/\" src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc` and\n   652\t  `grep -n \"ds/\" test/dao/space/index_test.cljc`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '298,410p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc | sed -n '935,980p;1050,1140p'\nnl -ba test/dao/space/transactor_test.cljc | sed -n '1,145p;250,430p;480,720p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '298,410p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc | sed -n '935,980p;1050,1140p'\nnl -ba test/dao/space/transactor_test.cljc | sed -n '1,145p;250,430p;480,720p'\"","aggregated_output":"   298\t## 3. Phase 1 — split index's payload vocabulary from its reading\n   299\t\n   300\t`src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc` and its test only; no behaviour change. It\n   301\tlands first because Phase 3 needs the vocabulary separable from the reader.\n   302\t\n   303\t1. Rename private `stream-payload-datoms` → private `element-datoms`. Body\n   304\t   unchanged; S3, S6, S7 preserved verbatim including both error messages.\n   305\t2. Add public `datoms-from-elements`: `(into [] (mapcat element-datoms)\n   306\t   elements)` — the local-stream payload vocabulary, one seq of elements to\n   307\t   canonical local d5 datoms. `into` is eager, so S6's throw-before-emission\n   308\t   ordering is unchanged.\n   309\t3. `snapshot-datoms` becomes drain-then-flatten over the existing v1 loop:\n   310\t   accumulate `(:ok result)` payloads, then `datoms-from-elements` on the\n   311\t   `:blocked`/`:end` exit. Gap and malformed-signal branches unchanged. S8 is\n   312\t   dropped here, with its reason.\n   313\t\n   314\t**Proof.** Add `datoms-from-elements-is-the-local-stream-vocabulary` to\n   315\t`index_test`, pinning S2, S3, S6, S7 directly rather than only through\n   316\t`publish-index!`: a bare datom passes through; a transaction record flattens;\n   317\textra keys / non-integer `:t` / empty `:datoms` / a datom whose `t` disagrees\n   318\twith the record all throw; a 5-vector with a non-namespaced `a` gets\n   319\t\"malformed local datom\"; anything else gets \"must be a datom or dao.space\n   320\ttransaction record\". Every existing snapshot test stays as written and now\n   321\tpins the drain and the composition rather than the vocabulary.\n   322\t\n   323\t## 4. Phase 2 — promote the snapshot loop to `dao.stream.observe/snapshot`\n   324\t\n   325\t1. `src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc`: add `snapshot` per D5. Amend the ns\n   326\t   docstring as D5 describes.\n   327\t2. `src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc`: `snapshot` becomes\n   328\t   `(let [{:keys [values] :as s} (observe/snapshot handle)]\n   329\t      (-> s (dissoc :values) (assoc :relation (relation values))))` — same\n   330\t   public shape, same statuses, loop deleted.\n   331\t3. `test/dao/stream/observe_test.cljc`: move query_test's status-coverage\n   332\t   cases (`snapshot-of-an-open-buffer-is-blocked` :339,\n   333\t   `snapshot-of-a-closed-buffer-ends` :350, `snapshot-of-a-gap-is-data` :359,\n   334\t   `snapshot-of-a-defect-carries-the-raw-answer` :386,\n   335\t   `snapshot-never-closes-the-handle` :402) down to `observe/snapshot`, where\n   336\t   they now belong, restating them over `:values`. `query_test` keeps\n   337\t   `snapshot-relation-feeds-current-and-q` (:410), which is the relation\n   338\t   wrapper's own property.\n   339\t\n   340\tThe second consumer arrives in Phase 3 of *this* plan, so this promotion is\n   341\tsequencing rather than speculation. Stated plainly because it is the one place\n   342\tthe index plan's rule (\"promote when the second consumer appears\") runs a\n   343\tphase early: if Phase 3 were abandoned, Phase 2 should be reverted with it.\n   344\t\n   345\t## 5. Phase 3 — the swap\n   346\t\n   347\tOne phase, because the constraint forbids leaving the `defopen` and\n   348\t`DaoStreamLog` half-deleted and every consumer breaks at the same instant.\n   349\t\n   350\t**`src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc`** — delete `DaoStreamLog` and\n   351\t`ds/defopen :transactor`; delete the `[dao.stream :as ds]` require and the\n   352\t`#?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream]))`.\n   353\t\n   354\t- `create!` per D2: validate the spec (reject `:next-t`; require a\n   355\t  `stream/reader?`-and-`stream/writer?` local stream; require a non-empty pool\n   356\t  of `stream/writer?` members — the pool check at :199-204 is already v2 and\n   357\t  moves verbatim), then `(derive-next-t (index/snapshot-datoms local-stream))`\n   358\t  and return `{:dao.space/transactor true :local-stream … :intake-pool …\n   359\t  :name … :next-t (atom t) :state (atom {:closed false})}`. A tag key,\n   360\t  following `:dao.space.query/published`.\n   361\t- `append-packet!` per D3: `stream/append!`, `stream/valid-outcome?`, advance\n   362\t  on `:dao.stream/ok` only, return the local outcome as data otherwise.\n   363\t- `append!` / `transact!` become plain functions over the value, keeping\n   364\t  `with-write-lock`, `val->datoms`, `entity->datoms`, `pad-datom` and\n   365\t  `derive-next-t` exactly as they are. The closed check returns\n   366\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` instead of throwing.\n   367\t- `close!` sets `:closed` inside the write lock and returns\n   368\t  `{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}`; idempotent.\n   369\t- `publish!` reads `(:local-stream log)` / `(:intake-pool log)` instead of\n   370\t  deftype fields.\n   371\t- No `next`, no `closed?`.\n   372\t\n   373\t**`src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc`** — `snapshot-datoms` becomes\n   374\t`observe/snapshot` + policy + `datoms-from-elements` per D5; add\n   375\t`[dao.stream.observe :as observe]`. `publish-index!`'s signature is\n   376\tunchanged; its `local-stream` is now a v2 handle. The `ds` require survives\n   377\tthis phase for the published adapter only, and dies in Phase 5.\n   378\t\n   379\t**`src/cljc/dao/space/schema.cljc`** — the six forced edits in D6's table,\n   380\tnothing else.\n   381\t\n   382\t**Tests.**\n   383\t\n   384\t- `transactor_test`: add `open-local` returning a v2 ringbuffer owner handle;\n   385\t  `open-with-intake` calls `transactor/create!`; the three test doubles\n   386\t  (`FailingAppendStream`, `ThrowingAppendStream`, the `close-linearizes`\n   387\t  `reify`) become v2 writers answering `{:dao.stream/outcome …}`; `tx-ts` and\n   388\t  the atomicity assertions read the local stream through the existing\n   389\t  `intake-values` loop, generalized to `stream-values`.\n   390\t  `readers-observe-atomic-transaction-records` (:382) and the read assertion\n   391\t  at :609 read `local` instead of `log` (T12). Receipt assertions take the D3\n   392\t  shape. `descriptor-validation` becomes `spec-validation`, its throw messages\n   393\t  following the constructor's wording.\n   394\t- `schema_test`, `stigmergy_test:106`, `index_test`'s `open-local`,\n   395\t  `query_test`'s `open-local` (:567), `schema_test:670`: v2 local streams,\n   396\t  under the rule in section 6.\n   397\t\n   398\t**Proof.** The unchanged deftests are the proof: `reopen-derives-next-t-from-\n   399\tretained-history` (:291) for T2, `malformed-or-gapped-retained-history-throws`\n   400\t(:317) for T4, `each-transaction-is-exactly-one-append` (:366) for T1,\n   401\t`append-failure-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry` (:499) and\n   402\t`append-throw-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry` (:515) for T5 — the first now\n   403\tobserving a returned outcome instead of a catch —\n   404\t`close-is-per-handle-and-does-not-touch-local-stream` (:584) for T7 and T13,\n   405\t`close-linearizes-after-an-in-flight-append` (:616) for T8,\n   406\t`single-writer-wrappers-are-not-coordinated` (:655) for T6,\n   407\t`publish-enqueues-indexes-into-the-pool` (:681) for T11. T14's replacement\n   408\tneeds a *new* case: an `append!` and a `transact!` after `close!` each answer\n   409\t`{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}` rather than throwing.\n   410\t\n   935\t  \"Serialize one wrapper's validate -> append -> state transition. The state\n   936\t   atom is a private per-wrapper coordination handle, never global state.\"\n   937\t  [lock f]\n   938\t  #?(:clj (locking lock (f))\n   939\t     :default (f)))\n   940\t\n   941\t\n   942\t(deftype SchemaWrapper\n   943\t  [inner local-stream strict? state]\n   944\t\n   945\t  ds/IDaoStreamBound\n   946\t\n   947\t  (close!\n   948\t    [_]\n   949\t    (with-write-lock state #(ds/close! inner)))\n   950\t\n   951\t\n   952\t  (closed?\n   953\t    [_]\n   954\t    (ds/closed? inner)))\n   955\t\n   956\t\n   957\t(defn transactor\n   958\t  \"Open a schema-validating wrapper over a local stream and intake pool.\n   959\t   opts: {:strict true} for strict mode (default lax). OWNS the inner\n   960\t   :transactor handle; closing the wrapper delegates inward.\"\n   961\t  ([local-stream intake-pool]\n   962\t   (transactor local-stream intake-pool nil))\n   963\t  ([local-stream intake-pool opts]\n   964\t   (let [strict? (boolean (:strict opts))\n   965\t         inner (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor\n   966\t                          :local-stream local-stream\n   967\t                          :intake-pool intake-pool\n   968\t                          :name \"schema\"})\n   969\t         rows (index/snapshot-datoms local-stream)\n   970\t         schema (extract-schema rows)]\n   971\t     (->SchemaWrapper inner local-stream strict?\n   972\t                      (atom (rows->state rows schema strict?))))))\n   973\t\n   974\t\n   975\t(defn- contains-schema-row?\n   976\t  \"True when any datom in the batch has an attribute that is one of the\n   977\t   five :db/* property names.\"\n   978\t  [datoms]\n   979\t  (some (fn [d] (schema-row? (second d))) datoms))\n   980\t\n  1050\t                               \" permits only its verbatim axiom facts, got \"\n  1051\t                               (pr-str [e a v]))\n  1052\t                          {:entity e, :ident ident, :attr a, :value v,\n  1053\t                           :expected (get expected a),\n  1054\t                           :operation (translated-op d)}))))))\n  1055\t  nil)\n  1056\t\n  1057\t\n  1058\t(defn transact!\n  1059\t  \"Translate, validate, and commit tx-data as one atomic record. Returns\n  1060\t   {:result :ok :t t :datoms datoms}. One per-wrapper serialized transition\n  1061\t   plans and validates the complete next state before the single append, then\n  1062\t   installs that already-planned state only after append succeeds. Schema\n  1063\t   changes become effective for the next transaction.\"\n  1064\t  [^SchemaWrapper wrapper tx-data]\n  1065\t  (let [lock (.-state wrapper)]\n  1066\t    (with-write-lock\n  1067\t      lock\n  1068\t      (fn []\n  1069\t        (when (ds/closed? wrapper)\n  1070\t          (throw (ex-info \"cannot transact! on closed wrapper\" {})))\n  1071\t        (when (empty? tx-data)\n  1072\t          (throw (ex-info \"transact! requires at least one item\"\n  1073\t                          {:tx-data tx-data})))\n  1074\t        (let [st @lock\n  1075\t              schema (:schema st)\n  1076\t              strict? (.-strict? wrapper)\n  1077\t              translated\n  1078\t              (loop [items (vec tx-data)\n  1079\t                     datoms []\n  1080\t                     state st]\n  1081\t                (if (empty? items)\n  1082\t                  {:datoms datoms, :state state}\n  1083\t                  (let [item (first items)\n  1084\t                        result (translate-record item state schema strict?)]\n  1085\t                    ;; Both-mode schema structure validation is part of the\n  1086\t                    ;; plan, before any append can occur.\n  1087\t                    (doseq [d (:datoms result)]\n  1088\t                      (validate-schema-row! (nth d 0) (nth d 1) (nth d 2)\n  1089\t                                            (:state result)))\n  1090\t                    (recur (rest items)\n  1091\t                           (into datoms (:datoms result))\n  1092\t                           (:state result)))))\n  1093\t              datoms (:datoms translated)]\n  1094\t          (when (empty? datoms)\n  1095\t            (throw (ex-info \"transact! produced no datoms\"\n  1096\t                            {:tx-data tx-data})))\n  1097\t          (validate-record-ops! datoms)\n  1098\t          (validate-axiom-datoms! datoms st)\n  1099\t          (let [schema-change? (boolean (contains-schema-row? datoms))\n  1100\t                next-schema (proposed-schema (.-local-stream wrapper)\n  1101\t                                             schema\n  1102\t                                             datoms)\n  1103\t                _ (validate-unique-card-one! next-schema)\n  1104\t                next-state (if schema-change?\n  1105\t                             (reindex-state (:state translated)\n  1106\t                                            next-schema\n  1107\t                                            strict?)\n  1108\t                             (-> (:state translated)\n  1109\t                                 (dissoc :datoms)\n  1110\t                                 (assoc :schema next-schema\n  1111\t                                        :strict? strict?)))\n  1112\t                result (tx/transact! (.-inner wrapper) datoms)]\n  1113\t            (reset! lock next-state)\n  1114\t            result))))))\n  1115\t\n  1116\t\n  1117\t;; =============================================================================\n  1118\t;; Publisher: publish! and published descriptor (§5)\n  1119\t;; =============================================================================\n  1120\t\n  1121\t(defn publish!\n  1122\t  \"Build and enqueue covered indexes over the wrapper's local stream.\n  1123\t   Thin passthrough to the inner handle's dao.space.transactor/publish!.\n  1124\t   Returns {:manifest-address ... :manifest ...}.\"\n  1125\t  ([^SchemaWrapper wrapper] (publish! wrapper nil))\n  1126\t  ([^SchemaWrapper wrapper opts]\n  1127\t   (when (ds/closed? wrapper)\n  1128\t     (throw (ex-info \"cannot publish! on closed wrapper\" {})))\n  1129\t   (tx/publish! (.-inner wrapper) opts)))\n  1130\t\n  1131\t\n  1132\t(defn published\n  1133\t  \"Construct a §5 published descriptor for one immutable covered-index\n  1134\t   manifest. content-store is a serializable DaoJing coordinate (map with\n  1135\t   :dao.jing/type); manifest-address is a segment content address.\n  1136\t   Validates like index/published-index but carries the schema type.\"\n  1137\t  [content-store manifest-address]\n  1138\t  (when-not (and (map? content-store) (keyword? (:dao.jing/type content-store)))\n  1139\t    (throw (ex-info \"published requires a DaoJing store coordinate\"\n  1140\t                    {:content-store content-store})))\n     1\t(ns dao.space.transactor-test\n     2\t  \"Contract tests for the :transactor stream (dao.space.transactor): a\n     3\t   single-writer wrapper over an explicit local dao.stream and an explicit\n     4\t   DaoJing intake pool (docs/design/dao.jing.md, Publication from an agent).\n     5\t\n     6\t   Every append!/transact! emits exactly ONE atomic transaction record\n     7\t   {:dao.space/transaction {:t n :datoms [...]}} through exactly one\n     8\t   ds/append!; t is owned by the wrapper and derived on open from the\n     9\t   retained history. publish! builds and enqueues the covered indexes into\n    10\t   the intake pool.\"\n    11\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    12\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    13\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    14\t            [dao.space.transactor :as transactor]\n    15\t            [dao.stream :as ds]\n    16\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer]\n    17\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    18\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    22\t;; Test doubles\n    23\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    24\t\n    25\t(defrecord ReaderOnlyStream\n    26\t  []\n    27\t\n    28\t  ds/IDaoStreamReader\n    29\t\n    30\t  (next [_this _cursor] :blocked))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(defrecord WriterOnlyStream\n    34\t  []\n    35\t\n    36\t  ds/IDaoStreamWriter\n    37\t\n    38\t  (append! [_this _val] {:result :ok}))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defrecord RecordingAppendStream\n    42\t  [inner records]\n    43\t\n    44\t  ds/IDaoStreamWriter\n    45\t\n    46\t  (append! [_this val] (swap! records conj val) (ds/append! inner val))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t  ds/IDaoStreamReader\n    50\t\n    51\t  (next [_this cursor] (ds/next inner cursor))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t  ds/IDaoStreamBound\n    55\t\n    56\t  (close! [_this] (ds/close! inner))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t  (closed? [_this] (ds/closed? inner)))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defrecord FailingAppendStream\n    63\t  [inner failures]\n    64\t\n    65\t  ds/IDaoStreamWriter\n    66\t\n    67\t  (append!\n    68\t    [_this packet]\n    69\t    (if (pos? (swap! failures dec))\n    70\t      {:result :full}\n    71\t      (ds/append! inner packet)))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t  ds/IDaoStreamReader\n    75\t\n    76\t  (next [_this cursor] (ds/next inner cursor))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t  ds/IDaoStreamBound\n    80\t\n    81\t  (close! [_this] (ds/close! inner))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t  (closed? [_this] (ds/closed? inner)))\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\t(defrecord ThrowingAppendStream\n    88\t  [inner throw?]\n    89\t\n    90\t  ds/IDaoStreamWriter\n    91\t\n    92\t  (append!\n    93\t    [_this _val]\n    94\t    (if @throw?\n    95\t      (do (reset! throw? false)\n    96\t          (throw (ex-info \"simulated transport failure\" {})))\n    97\t      (ds/append! inner val)))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t  ds/IDaoStreamReader\n   101\t\n   102\t  (next [_this cursor] (ds/next inner cursor))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t  ds/IDaoStreamBound\n   106\t\n   107\t  (close! [_this] (ds/close! inner))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t  (closed? [_this] (ds/closed? inner)))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   114\t;; Helpers\n   115\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn- open-intake\n   118\t  \"A dao.stream ringbuffer intake writer.\"\n   119\t  [capacity]\n   120\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n   121\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n   122\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn- intake-values\n   126\t  \"Every value currently on a v2 intake stream, read from its oldest\n   127\t   cursor — the test's view of what publication enqueued.\"\n   128\t  [s]\n   129\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor s :dao.stream/oldest))\n   130\t         acc []]\n   131\t    (let [r (stream/next s cursor)]\n   132\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   133\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   134\t        acc))))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(defn- open-with-intake\n   138\t  ([local] (open-with-intake local (open-intake 4096)))\n   139\t  ([local intake]\n   140\t   (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   141\t              :local-stream local,\n   142\t              :intake-pool [intake]})))\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn- content-handle\n   250\t                              #\"IDaoStreamWriter\"\n   251\t              (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   252\t                         :local-stream local,\n   253\t                         :intake-pool [42]})))))\n   254\t    (testing \":name is optional and diagnostic only\"\n   255\t      (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})]\n   256\t        (is (some? (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   257\t                              :local-stream local,\n   258\t                              :intake-pool [intake]})))\n   259\t        (is (some? (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   260\t                              :local-stream local,\n   261\t                              :intake-pool [intake],\n   262\t                              :name \"producer\"})))))\n   263\t    (testing \":next-t cannot override history-derived causality\"\n   264\t      (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})]\n   265\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   266\t                                 :clj Exception\n   267\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   268\t                              #\"next-t\"\n   269\t              (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   270\t                         :local-stream local,\n   271\t                         :intake-pool [intake],\n   272\t                         :next-t 99})))))\n   273\t    (testing \"opening creates, registers, or closes nothing\"\n   274\t      (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   275\t            pool (open-intake 4096)]\n   276\t        (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   277\t                   :local-stream local,\n   278\t                   :intake-pool [pool]})\n   279\t        (is (false? (ds/closed? local)))\n   280\t        (is (empty? (ds/->seq nil local)))\n   281\t        (is (empty? (intake-values pool)))\n   282\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   283\t               (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! pool ::probe)))\n   284\t            \"the intake pool was neither closed nor written by the open\")))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   288\t;; Transaction time derivation\n   289\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   290\t\n   291\t(deftest reopen-derives-next-t-from-retained-history\n   292\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   293\t        intake (open-intake 4096)\n   294\t        a (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   295\t                     :local-stream local,\n   296\t                     :intake-pool [intake]})]\n   297\t    (is (= {:result :ok, :t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   298\t           (ds/append! a {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})))\n   299\t    (transactor/transact! a [{:db/id 2, :test/b 2} {:db/id 3, :test/c 3}])\n   300\t    (testing \"a reopened wrapper derives 1 + max retained datom t\"\n   301\t      (let [b (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   302\t                         :local-stream local,\n   303\t                         :intake-pool [intake]})]\n   304\t        (is (= {:result :ok, :t 2, :datoms [[4 :test/d 4 2 1]]}\n   305\t               (ds/append! b {:db/id 4, :test/d 4})))\n   306\t        (is (= #{0 1 2} (set (tx-ts local)))\n   307\t            \"the scan read, and did not consume, the retained history\")))\n   308\t    (testing \"an empty local stream derives 0\"\n   309\t      (let [fresh (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   310\t            c (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   311\t                         :local-stream fresh,\n   312\t                         :intake-pool [intake]})]\n   313\t        (is (= {:result :ok, :t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   314\t               (ds/append! c {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})))))))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\t(deftest malformed-or-gapped-retained-history-throws\n   318\t  (let [intake (open-intake 4096)\n   319\t        open-on (fn [local]\n   320\t                  (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   321\t                             :local-stream local,\n   322\t                             :intake-pool [intake]}))]\n   323\t    (testing \"a retention gap at cursor zero throws on open\"\n   324\t      (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer,\n   325\t                             :capacity 2,\n   326\t                             :eviction-policy :evict-oldest})]\n   327\t        (doseq [i (range 3)]\n   328\t          (ds/append! local\n   329\t                      {:dao.space/transaction {:t i,\n   330\t                                               :datoms [[i :test/a i i 1]]}}))\n   331\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   332\t                                 :clj Exception\n   333\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   334\t                              #\"gap\"\n   335\t              (open-on local)))))\n   336\t    (testing \"a malformed payload in the retained history throws on open\"\n   337\t      (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})]\n   338\t        (ds/append! local 42)\n   339\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   340\t                                 :clj Exception\n   341\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   342\t                              #\"payload\"\n   343\t              (open-on local)))))\n   344\t    (testing \"an out-of-shape transaction record throws on open\"\n   345\t      (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})]\n   346\t        (ds/append! local {:dao.space/transaction {:t 1, :datoms :nope}})\n   347\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   348\t                                 :clj Exception\n   349\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   350\t                              #\"transaction\"\n   351\t              (open-on local)))))\n   352\t    (testing \"a non-integer datom t in the retained history throws on open\"\n   353\t      (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})]\n   354\t        (ds/append! local [1 :test/a :v :bogus 1])\n   355\t        (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   356\t                                 :clj Exception\n   357\t                                 :cljs js/Error)\n   358\t                              #\"integer\"\n   359\t              (open-on local)))))))\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   363\t;; Atomic packet shape\n   364\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   365\t\n   366\t(deftest each-transaction-is-exactly-one-append\n   367\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   368\t        recording (->RecordingAppendStream local (atom []))\n   369\t        log (open-with-intake recording)]\n   370\t    (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})\n   371\t    (transactor/transact! log [{:db/id 2, :test/b 2} {:db/id 3, :test/c 3}])\n   372\t    (is\n   373\t      (= [{:dao.space/transaction {:t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}}\n   374\t          {:dao.space/transaction\n   375\t           {:t 1, :datoms [[2 :test/b 2 1 1] [3 :test/c 3 1 1]]}}]\n   376\t         @(:records recording))\n   377\t      \"two transactions, exactly two underlying ds/append! calls — no torn\n   378\t         packet, no extra calls\")\n   379\t    (is (= 2 (count @(:records recording))))))\n   380\t\n   381\t\n   382\t(deftest readers-observe-atomic-transaction-records\n   383\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   384\t        log (open-with-intake local)]\n   385\t    (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})\n   386\t    (transactor/transact! log [{:db/id 2, :test/b 2}])\n   387\t    (let [r1 (ds/next log {:position 0})\n   388\t          r2 (ds/next log (:cursor r1))]\n   389\t      (is (= {:dao.space/transaction {:t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}}\n   390\t             (:ok r1)))\n   391\t      (is (= {:dao.space/transaction {:t 1, :datoms [[2 :test/b 2 1 1]]}}\n   392\t             (:ok r2)))\n   393\t      (is (= :blocked (ds/next log (:cursor r2))))\n   394\t      (is (= [{:dao.space/transaction {:t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}}\n   395\t              {:dao.space/transaction {:t 1, :datoms [[2 :test/b 2 1 1]]}}]\n   396\t             (vec (ds/->seq nil local)))\n   397\t          \"readers of the local stream see the same atomic records\"))))\n   398\t\n   399\t\n   400\t(deftest concurrent-calls-on-one-wrapper-serialize-transaction-time\n   401\t  #?(:clj (let [inner (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   402\t                slow-local\n   403\t                (reify\n   404\t                  ds/IDaoStreamWriter\n   405\t                  (append! [_ val] (Thread/sleep 5) (ds/append! inner val))\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t                  ds/IDaoStreamReader\n   409\t\n   410\t                  (next [_ cursor] (ds/next inner cursor)))\n   411\t                log (open-with-intake slow-local)\n   412\t                start (promise)\n   413\t                calls (mapv (fn [i]\n   414\t                              (future @start\n   415\t                                      (ds/append! log\n   416\t                                                  {:db/id (+ 16 i),\n   417\t                                                   :test/value i})))\n   418\t                            (range 32))]\n   419\t            (deliver start true)\n   420\t            (run! deref calls)\n   421\t            (is (= (set (range 32)) (set (tx-ts inner)))\n   422\t                \"one wrapper is one serialized writer even when callers race\"))\n   423\t     :default (is true\n   424\t                  \"shared-memory concurrency is a JVM-only execution mode\")))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   428\t;; Entity expansion\n   429\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   430\t\n   480\t             (ds/append! log [5 :test/e 5]))))\n   481\t    (testing \"a value that is neither entity map nor datom vector throws\"\n   482\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   483\t                               :clj Exception\n   484\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   485\t                            #\"entity map or datom\"\n   486\t            (ds/append! log 42))))\n   487\t    (testing \"an input that produces zero datoms is rejected\"\n   488\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   489\t                               :clj Exception\n   490\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   491\t                            #\"no datoms\"\n   492\t            (ds/append! log {:db/id 1}))))))\n   493\t\n   494\t\n   495\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   496\t;; Failure handling\n   497\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   498\t\n   499\t(deftest append-failure-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry\n   500\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   501\t        flaky (->FailingAppendStream local (atom 2))\n   502\t        log (open-with-intake flaky)]\n   503\t    (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   504\t                             :clj Exception\n   505\t                             :cljs js/Error)\n   506\t                          #\"failed\"\n   507\t          (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})))\n   508\t    (is (= {:result :ok, :t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   509\t           (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))\n   510\t        \"retry lands at the same t: the failed append never advanced it\")\n   511\t    (is (= {:result :ok, :t 1, :datoms [[2 :test/b 2 1 1]]}\n   512\t           (ds/append! log {:db/id 2, :test/b 2})))))\n   513\t\n   514\t\n   515\t(deftest append-throw-does-not-advance-t-and-can-retry\n   516\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   517\t        throwing (->ThrowingAppendStream local (atom true))\n   518\t        log (open-with-intake throwing)]\n   519\t    (is (thrown? #?(:cljd Object\n   520\t                    :clj Exception\n   521\t                    :cljs js/Error)\n   522\t          (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})))\n   523\t    (is (= {:result :ok, :t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   524\t           (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))\n   525\t        \"a thrown underlying error leaves the watermark unchanged\")))\n   526\t\n   527\t\n   528\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   529\t;; transact!\n   530\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   531\t\n   532\t(deftest transact-commits-one-atomic-record\n   533\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   534\t        log (open-with-intake local)]\n   535\t    (testing \"several items commit under one t in one atomic record\"\n   536\t      (let [{:keys [result t datoms]}\n   537\t            (transactor/transact! log\n   538\t                                  [{:db/id 100, :test/a 1}\n   539\t                                   {:db/id 101, :test/b 2} [102 :test/c 3]])]\n   540\t        (is (= :ok result))\n   541\t        (is (= 0 t))\n   542\t        (is (= 3 (count datoms)))\n   543\t        (is (apply = (map #(nth % 3) datoms))\n   544\t            \"every datom in the batch shares one t\")\n   545\t        (is (= [[100 :test/a 1 0 1] [101 :test/b 2 0 1] [102 :test/c 3 0 1]]\n   546\t               datoms)))\n   547\t      (is (= [{:dao.space/transaction {:t 0,\n   548\t                                       :datoms [[100 :test/a 1 0 1]\n   549\t                                                [101 :test/b 2 0 1]\n   550\t                                                [102 :test/c 3 0 1]]}}]\n   551\t             (vec (ds/->seq nil local)))\n   552\t          \"exactly one atomic packet on the stream\"))\n   553\t    (testing \"a transact! after an append! gets a distinct t\"\n   554\t      (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})\n   555\t      (is (= {:result :ok, :t 2, :datoms [[2 :test/b 2 2 1]]}\n   556\t             (transactor/transact! log [{:db/id 2, :test/b 2}]))))\n   557\t    (testing \"an empty tx-data collection throws\"\n   558\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   559\t                               :clj Exception\n   560\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   561\t                            #\"at least one\"\n   562\t            (transactor/transact! log []))))\n   563\t    (testing \"an expansion producing zero datoms throws\"\n   564\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   565\t                               :clj Exception\n   566\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   567\t                            #\"no datoms\"\n   568\t            (transactor/transact! log [{:db/id 1}]))))\n   569\t    (testing \"an invalid item throws before any append — no partial prefix\"\n   570\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   571\t                               :clj Exception\n   572\t                               :cljs js/Error)\n   573\t                            #\"entity map or datom\"\n   574\t            (transactor/transact! log\n   575\t                                  [{:db/id 1, :test/a 1} 42])))\n   576\t      (is (= 3 (count (ds/->seq nil local)))\n   577\t          \"the invalid batch appended nothing\"))))\n   578\t\n   579\t\n   580\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   581\t;; Close ownership\n   582\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   583\t\n   584\t(deftest close-is-per-handle-and-does-not-touch-local-stream\n   585\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   586\t        intake (open-intake 4096)\n   587\t        log (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   588\t                       :local-stream local,\n   589\t                       :intake-pool [intake]})]\n   590\t    (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})\n   591\t    (is (false? (ds/closed? log)))\n   592\t    (is (= {:woke []} (ds/close! log)))\n   593\t    (is (true? (ds/closed? log)))\n   594\t    (is (false? (ds/closed? local))\n   595\t        \"closing the wrapper must not close the supplied local stream\")\n   596\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   597\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! intake ::probe)))\n   598\t        \"closing the wrapper must not close the supplied intake pool\")\n   599\t    (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   600\t                             :clj Exception\n   601\t                             :cljs js/Error)\n   602\t                          #\"closed\"\n   603\t          (ds/append! log {:db/id 2, :test/a 2})))\n   604\t    (is (thrown-with-msg? #?(:cljd Object\n   605\t                             :clj Exception\n   606\t                             :cljs js/Error)\n   607\t                          #\"closed\"\n   608\t          (transactor/transact! log [{:db/id 2, :test/a 2}])))\n   609\t    (is (map? (ds/next log {:position 0}))\n   610\t        \"the wrapper still delegates reads after close\")\n   611\t    (is (= [{:dao.space/transaction {:t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}}]\n   612\t           (vec (ds/->seq nil local)))\n   613\t        \"closing neither closes nor erases the local stream\")))\n   614\t\n   615\t\n   616\t(deftest close-linearizes-after-an-in-flight-append\n   617\t  #?(:clj (let [inner (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   618\t                entered (promise)\n   619\t                release (promise)\n   620\t                slow-local (reify\n   621\t                             ds/IDaoStreamWriter\n   622\t                             (append!\n   623\t                               [_ packet]\n   624\t                               (deliver entered true)\n   625\t                               @release\n   626\t                               (ds/append! inner packet))\n   627\t\n   628\t\n   629\t                             ds/IDaoStreamReader\n   630\t\n   631\t                             (next [_ cursor] (ds/next inner cursor)))\n   632\t                log (open-with-intake slow-local)\n   633\t                writing (future (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :test/a 1}))]\n   634\t            @entered\n   635\t            (let [closing (future (ds/close! log))]\n   636\t              (try (is (= ::timeout (deref closing 50 ::timeout))\n   637\t                       \"close waits for the serialized write boundary\")\n   638\t                   (finally (deliver release true)))\n   639\t              (is (= {:result :ok, :t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]} @writing))\n   640\t              (is (= {:woke []} @closing))\n   641\t              (is (true? (ds/closed? log)))\n   642\t              (is (thrown-with-msg? Exception\n   643\t                                    #\"closed\"\n   644\t                    (ds/append! log {:db/id 2, :test/a 2})))\n   645\t              (is (= 1 (count (ds/->seq nil inner)))\n   646\t                  \"no append crosses the point at which close returns\")))\n   647\t     :default (is true\n   648\t                  \"shared-memory close races are a JVM-only execution mode\")))\n   649\t\n   650\t\n   651\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   652\t;; Single-writer\n   653\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   654\t\n   655\t(deftest single-writer-wrappers-are-not-coordinated\n   656\t  (testing\n   657\t    \"two wrappers over the same local stream each derive the same\n   658\t            next-t and silently write colliding records: documented hazard,\n   659\t            no coordination is possible without shared mutable state\"\n   660\t    (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   661\t          intake (open-intake 4096)\n   662\t          a (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   663\t                       :local-stream local,\n   664\t                       :intake-pool [intake]})\n   665\t          b (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   666\t                       :local-stream local,\n   667\t                       :intake-pool [intake]})]\n   668\t      (is (= {:result :ok, :t 0, :datoms [[1 :test/a 1 0 1]]}\n   669\t             (ds/append! a {:db/id 1, :test/a 1})))\n   670\t      (is (= {:result :ok, :t 0, :datoms [[2 :test/b 2 0 1]]}\n   671\t             (ds/append! b {:db/id 2, :test/b 2}))\n   672\t          \"wrapper b independently derived t=0 from the same history\")\n   673\t      (is (= #{0} (set (tx-ts local)))\n   674\t          \"two colliding records at t=0, not a sequential log\"))))\n   675\t\n   676\t\n   677\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   678\t;; publish!\n   679\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   680\t\n   681\t(deftest publish-enqueues-indexes-into-the-pool\n   682\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   683\t        a (open-intake 1024)\n   684\t        b (open-intake 1024)\n   685\t        log (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :transactor,\n   686\t                       :local-stream local,\n   687\t                       :intake-pool [a b]})]\n   688\t    (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :work/status :todo})\n   689\t    (ds/append! log {:db/id 2, :work/status :done})\n   690\t    (testing \"publish! returns the manifest and its content address\"\n   691\t      (let [{:keys [manifest-address manifest]} (transactor/publish! log)]\n   692\t        (is (= \"segment\" (namespace manifest-address)))\n   693\t        (is (= manifest-address (jing/segment-key manifest)))\n   694\t        (is (= #{:indexes :count :branching-factor} (set (keys manifest))))\n   695\t        (is (= 2 (:count manifest)))\n   696\t        (is (seq (intake-values a)) \"the default :select-stream is first\")\n   697\t        (is (empty? (intake-values b)))))\n   698\t    (testing \"publication touches no stream lifecycle\"\n   699\t      (is (false? (ds/closed? local)))\n   700\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! a ::probe)))\n   701\t          \"intake a was not closed\")\n   702\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! b ::probe)))\n   703\t          \"intake b was not closed\"))\n   704\t    (testing \"opts route through: :select-stream picks the pool member\"\n   705\t      (let [{:keys [manifest]} (transactor/publish! log\n   706\t                                                    {:select-stream second})]\n   707\t        (is (= 2 (:count manifest)))\n   708\t        (is (seq (intake-values b)))))\n   709\t    (testing \"opts route through: :branching-factor\"\n   710\t      (let [{:keys [manifest]} (transactor/publish! log {:branching-factor 16})]\n   711\t        (is (= 16 (:branching-factor manifest)))))\n   712\t    (testing \"publish! does not consume the local stream\"\n   713\t      (is (= 2 (count (ds/->seq nil local)))))))\n   714\t\n   715\t\n   716\t(deftest publish-materializes-through-observer-and-reads-back\n   717\t  (let [local (ds/open! {:dao.stream/type :ringbuffer})\n   718\t        intake (open-intake 1024)\n   719\t        log (open-with-intake local intake)]\n   720\t    (ds/append! log {:db/id 1, :work/status :todo})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
